-- GAME ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Title       Game Over 2 (aka Phantis), part 1
  Publisher   Dinamic, 1988
  Version     1.0

-- YOU NEED ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Your own copy of the original game, saved beside this patch:

  File        Game Over 2 (1988)(Dinamic)(ES)(en)(Part 1 of 2)[aka
              Phantis][re-release].z80
  MD5         c39caed696ba547f693546b707c9cee8

  The patch carries none of the game's code. It only works with that exact
  dump, under that name or any other: anything else is refused, with a
  message naming the file it wants.

  Memory      Any Next: a 1MB Next has the memory for the game. Enhanced needs
              a 1MB Next, and is not offered on a smaller one.

-- WHAT IT DOES --------------------------------------------------------------
  Moving figures are drawn on the Next's own graphics layers, so they keep their
  own colours and no longer take on the scenery's (colour clash). Game logic is
  unchanged.

  Colours     Default (the game's own) plus: Enhanced, chosen on the menu, off
              by default.
  Enhanced    The Spec256 colours on every figure this release shares with the
              set: the player's ship, shots, explosions, scenery. Others stay
              in the original's colours. Source: Enhanced colours: David Goti
              (Spec256).

  Pace        original

  Changes     1.0: figures in their own colours on a double-buffered Layer 2,
              in the game's own plot order, over the original bitmap; scenery
              in its own attributes; the plot runs whole at 28 MHz in pace
              windows; the tape's loading screen; Sinclair's 48K ROM as the
              whole alt ROM (NextZXOS 26.11 safe); the game's speed restored
              after every hook; R kept as the original's; Enhanced colours, a
              menu option, off by default, from the Spec256 set by David Goti,
              as they are

  Note        Keys: on the game's menu K keyboard (it asks for right, left,
              up, down, fire, abort, pause), J Kempston joystick, S start;
              hold the key a moment. Default: the original look, figures in
              their own colours, scenery in its own. Enhanced (off): the
              Spec256 colours on every figure the set has. Fits a 1MB Next.
              Known issues: pace in JNext against the original over 800
              updates, 5 seeds, game state in lockstep: default -0.64 to
              -0.08%, quiet thirds +0.19 to +1.23%, busy thirds -1.57 to
              -0.85%, slowest 20 updates up to +6.75%; Enhanced -1.83 to
              -1.45%, quiet thirds -1.23 to -0.72%, busy thirds -2.83 to
              -2.39%, slowest 20 updates +4.33%. In Enhanced much of the art
              stays in the original's colours, where this release redrew it:
              fighters, yellow ships, asteroids, part of the scenery, the end
              scene, ZONE numbers; and the panel. Missing: Enhanced's nebula
              backdrop; natural play to the end; hardware untested.

-- MENU ----------------------------------------------------------------------
   1  Infinite lives

  The archive's POKE for this release, tested alone in the simulator, same
  keys with and without it: lives never fall (3 lost without it). Left out:
  Enable invisible mode (no effect in testing).

